of the sweet one, who was a bitter foe to the kings with many spears and majestic elephants!","modern":"ஒரு பக்கத்தில் அருவிகள் ஆரவாரம் செய்ய, மற்றொரு பக்கத்தில் பாணர்களுடைய பாத்திரங்கள் நிறையும்படி ஊற்றும்போது சிதறிய இனிய கள் தெளிவு பாறைகளில் மோதி ஓடும். பல வேல்களையும் பெருமை பொருந்திய யானைகளையும் உடைய பகை வேந்தர்களுக்கு இன்னாதவனாகவும், நமக்கு இனியவனாகவும் இருந்த பாரியினுடைய பறம்பு மலை இத்தகைய சிறப்புடையதாக இருந்ததுவே!","explanation":"This poem is a lament (kaiyaṟunilai) composed by the poet Kapilar after the death of his patron and close friend, Vēḷ Pāri. The poet recalls the past glory of Pāri's hill, Parampu Malai, contrasting its former abundance with its current state of loss. On one side of the hill, natural waterfalls roared, while on the other side, the abundance of sweet toddy poured for visiting bards was so immense that the overflow ran down like a stream, washing over the rocks. Pāri was a terrifying, unyielding foe to the powerful crowned kings who besieged him, yet he was incredibly sweet and generous to the poets and bards who sought his patronage. The particle 'maṉṉē' highlights the deep grief of the poet, emphasizing that this magnificent sight is now only a memory.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.4],[0.4,0.6],[0.6,0.86],[0.86,1.2],[1.2,1.8],[1.8,2.16],[2.16,2.7],[2.7,2.9],[2.9,3.5],[3.5,4.25],[4.25,4.53],[4.53,4.8],[4.8,5.0],[5.0,5.4],[5.4,5.73],[5.73,6.4],[6.4,6.6],[6.6,7.0],[7.0,7.4],[7.4,7.7],[7.7,8.3],[8.3,8.6],[8.6,9.1],[9.1,10.51],[10.51,10.83],[10.83,11.14],[11.14,11.44]],"female":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.63],[1.63,1.9],[1.9,2.3],[2.3,2.9],[2.9,3.1],[3.1,3.3],[3.3,3.8],[3.8,4.3],[4.3,4.8],[4.8,5.13],[5.13,5.47],[5.47,5.97],[5.97,6.97],[6.97,7.63],[7.63,8.13],[8.13,8.47],[8.47,8.8],[8.8,9.47],[9.47,9.8],[9.8,10.3],[10.3,11.1],[11.1,11.7],[11.7,12.6],[12.6,12.93]]},"sync":[[["ஒரு","one"]],[["சார்","side"]],[["அருவி","waterfall"]],[["ஆர்ப்ப","roaring"]],[["ஒரு","one"]],[["சார்","side"]],[["பாணர்","bards"]],[[